invariant: INV-14
file: webpki_ticket.c
catches: webpki_resume_test
reason: the configuration hash takes the hostname's bytes as they are, so a
  ticket fails to resume under the same name written with different
  capitals, though the chain walk treats the two as one name
  (RFC 6125 section 6.4.1). The capitals rows object.

--- old
    return c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z' ? (uint8_t)(c + ('a' - 'A')) : c;
--- new
    return c;
